1
00:00:11,503 --> 00:00:13,176
Look at a colour in front of you.

2
00:00:13,256 --> 00:00:15,830
Now ask: who is doing the seeing?

3
00:00:16,633 --> 00:00:21,747
This is After Anatta: notes by
John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:22,578 --> 00:00:25,080
When I look back over
my books and articles,

5
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:27,199
the same move keeps turning up.

6
00:00:27,279 --> 00:00:32,281
Something seems to stand behind an
action, doing it. A seer behind seeing.

7
00:00:32,361 --> 00:00:33,979
A walker behind walking.

8
00:00:34,059 --> 00:00:36,941
A cause behind its effect, pushing it out.

9
00:00:37,021 --> 00:00:40,202
A ground behind appearances,
giving them off.

10
00:00:40,282 --> 00:00:43,273
Each time it is looked
for, it is not found.

11
00:00:43,353 --> 00:00:46,470
And each time, nothing
is put in its place.

12
00:00:47,289 --> 00:00:52,277
Anatta, dependent arising and spontaneous
presence are three names for that one

13
00:00:52,357 --> 00:00:55,021
finding. Anatta makes it in seeing.

14
00:00:55,101 --> 00:00:57,413
Dependent arising makes it everywhere.

15
00:00:57,493 --> 00:01:02,879
Spontaneous presence is what is met when
nothing is left that makes the appearing.

16
00:01:03,698 --> 00:01:07,559
So they are not three teachings,
and they are not three stages.

17
00:01:07,639 --> 00:01:10,018
They are three descriptions of one taste.

18
00:01:10,098 --> 00:01:12,436
Anatta says no one is behind it.

19
00:01:12,516 --> 00:01:16,118
Dependent arising says nothing
in it stands on its own.

20
00:01:16,198 --> 00:01:19,624
Spontaneous presence
says nothing is missing,

21
00:01:19,704 --> 00:01:21,435
and nothing is making it.

22
00:01:22,241 --> 00:01:23,959
This talk has two parts.

23
00:01:24,075 --> 00:01:27,161
First the journey, in
which the taste is met.

24
00:01:27,241 --> 00:01:29,869
Then the map, in which it is described.

25
00:01:30,669 --> 00:01:32,686
The journey starts with anatta.

26
00:01:33,518 --> 00:01:37,446
The Buddha told Bāhiya: in
the seen, just the seen.

27
00:01:37,526 --> 00:01:40,508
No one behind the eyes, doing the seeing.

28
00:01:41,322 --> 00:01:42,438
Think of the wind.

29
00:01:42,518 --> 00:01:47,139
We say the wind is blowing, as if the wind
were one thing and the blowing another

30
00:01:47,219 --> 00:01:53,219
thing it does. But when the blowing stops,
no wind is left over, resting somewhere.

31
00:01:53,632 --> 00:01:55,278
The blowing is the wind.

32
00:01:55,358 --> 00:02:00,024
In the same way, there is seeing,
and no seer left over behind it.

33
00:02:00,825 --> 00:02:05,160
When the witness is not found,
experience does not go blank.

34
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:07,923
The tree is more vivid, not less.

35
00:02:08,738 --> 00:02:10,778
But anatta does not do everything.

36
00:02:10,858 --> 00:02:13,074
It removes the one who watches.

37
00:02:13,154 --> 00:02:16,919
It does not, by itself,
remove the things watched.

38
00:02:16,999 --> 00:02:20,646
The observer has disappeared,
but the world has not.

39
00:02:20,736 --> 00:02:24,383
Things, causes and time
can still be held as solid,

40
00:02:24,472 --> 00:02:26,448
each sitting there by itself.

41
00:02:27,257 --> 00:02:29,994
Right after anatta comes a first taste.

42
00:02:30,813 --> 00:02:33,518
What are seeing and hearing, in real time?

43
00:02:33,598 --> 00:02:36,018
We call them events, processes.

44
00:02:36,098 --> 00:02:39,637
That is true, but it is
still words. So look.

45
00:02:40,441 --> 00:02:46,343
Seeing is just colours. No effort at all.
Hearing is just sound. No effort at all.

46
00:02:47,141 --> 00:02:51,082
Nothing is doing the seeing, and
the seeing is not being done.

47
00:02:51,162 --> 00:02:54,928
Even what we called a process
does not seem to be a process.

48
00:02:55,008 --> 00:03:00,380
Nothing runs underneath the colours,
carrying them from one moment to the next.

49
00:03:01,185 --> 00:03:02,885
And the colours are not dark.

50
00:03:02,965 --> 00:03:05,398
They are clear, known and vivid.

51
00:03:05,478 --> 00:03:07,450
The knowing is right there in the colour,

52
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:10,253
and nothing stands behind it, knowing.

53
00:03:11,053 --> 00:03:13,935
At the same time, the
factors are intimate.

54
00:03:14,015 --> 00:03:18,269
The colour is there only with
light, with the eye, with attention.

55
00:03:18,349 --> 00:03:22,888
The sound is there only with the
air, the ear, and the car going by.

56
00:03:22,968 --> 00:03:25,769
None of these stands
outside, feeding it in.

57
00:03:25,849 --> 00:03:28,853
The alignment of these
factors is the appearing.

58
00:03:28,933 --> 00:03:32,617
Not two steps, factors
first and then a lining up.

59
00:03:32,697 --> 00:03:36,167
They are how we speak of the
appearing when we take it apart.

60
00:03:36,990 --> 00:03:42,481
So here, right after anatta, is a
first-hand taste of spontaneous presence.

61
00:03:42,561 --> 00:03:44,999
Remember it. I will come back to it.

62
00:03:45,813 --> 00:03:49,157
How is this different from
a refined non-dual state?

63
00:03:49,237 --> 00:03:52,173
A refined non-dual rests in oneness.

64
00:03:52,253 --> 00:03:54,483
It is still haunted by substance.

65
00:03:54,563 --> 00:03:58,110
It thinks of everything
as made of one luminosity,

66
00:03:58,190 --> 00:04:01,376
one clarity that colours
and sounds are made of.

67
00:04:02,185 --> 00:04:05,121
Oneness merges the seer into everything.

68
00:04:05,201 --> 00:04:07,757
Anatta finds no seer there to merge.

69
00:04:07,837 --> 00:04:12,666
With nothing merged, no "one" is
left for everything to be made of.

70
00:04:13,469 --> 00:04:15,970
In the taste, there is no "made of".

71
00:04:16,050 --> 00:04:17,913
The colour is clear as colour.

72
00:04:17,993 --> 00:04:19,761
The sound is clear as sound.

73
00:04:19,841 --> 00:04:22,288
Each is complete with its own conditions.

74
00:04:22,368 --> 00:04:26,337
Six clarities, one for each
of the senses and the mind,

75
00:04:26,417 --> 00:04:28,719
not one lamp lighting them all.

76
00:04:29,529 --> 00:04:33,756
So the test is simple. Is there a
"one" that everything is made of?

77
00:04:33,836 --> 00:04:36,165
If so, substance is still there.

78
00:04:36,986 --> 00:04:40,045
This taste does not stay
in seeing and hearing.

79
00:04:40,125 --> 00:04:45,865
After anatta it widens, often by
itself, before I had any view for it.

80
00:04:46,673 --> 00:04:49,378
Each event seems to
spend itself completely.

81
00:04:49,458 --> 00:04:52,422
The sound of a car going
by is wholly the sound.

82
00:04:52,502 --> 00:04:54,894
Nothing is behind it, holding back.

83
00:04:54,974 --> 00:04:59,555
Boundaries lose their solidity,
yet distinctions never disappear.

84
00:04:59,635 --> 00:05:01,176
The car is still the car.

85
00:05:02,002 --> 00:05:07,045
Dōgen called this total exertion: each
thing spending itself fully in its own

86
00:05:07,125 --> 00:05:08,159
place.

87
00:05:08,239 --> 00:05:12,497
Firewood in its place, ash
in its place, each complete.

88
00:05:13,297 --> 00:05:19,297
It is easily heard as "the whole cosmos is
present in each moment". That is holism.

89
00:05:19,479 --> 00:05:22,863
It only makes the whole the
ground instead of the parts.

90
00:05:22,943 --> 00:05:27,868
The event spends itself completely,
with no cosmos packed inside it.

91
00:05:28,685 --> 00:05:30,344
It is not a second taste.

92
00:05:30,424 --> 00:05:34,026
It is the same taste,
widening beyond the senses.

93
00:05:34,106 --> 00:05:38,401
In seeing and hearing I spoke
of it as spontaneous presence.

94
00:05:38,481 --> 00:05:42,029
Spreading through each
event, it is total exertion.

95
00:05:42,109 --> 00:05:44,737
Already two descriptions of one taste.

96
00:05:45,574 --> 00:05:47,537
But a taste is not yet freedom.

97
00:05:48,349 --> 00:05:53,377
All of this is the taste:
immediate, effortless, spontaneous.

98
00:05:53,457 --> 00:05:57,073
And still the mind has not
released its habit of reifying.

99
00:05:57,153 --> 00:05:59,183
Ignorance has not been unbound.

100
00:05:59,993 --> 00:06:01,842
How can both be there at once?

101
00:06:01,922 --> 00:06:03,989
Because they are not in the same place.

102
00:06:04,069 --> 00:06:07,413
The taste is in the
immediacy of the senses.

103
00:06:07,493 --> 00:06:10,936
The habit is in how the world
is understood around it.

104
00:06:11,757 --> 00:06:16,582
While I see a flower, the seeing is
just colours, with no one behind it.

105
00:06:16,662 --> 00:06:20,902
Yet the moment I turn away, the flower
is still assumed to be sitting there by

106
00:06:20,982 --> 00:06:23,633
itself, its red belonging to it.

107
00:06:23,713 --> 00:06:26,459
A cause is still felt to push its effect.

108
00:06:26,539 --> 00:06:28,801
Death is still the end of a someone.

109
00:06:29,698 --> 00:06:34,482
For years after anatta, the taste was
there and the view still treated each

110
00:06:34,562 --> 00:06:36,928
thing as standing by itself.

111
00:06:37,008 --> 00:06:39,958
That gap is what I call
the desynchronisation.

112
00:06:40,038 --> 00:06:44,256
The experience is free of
substance. The framework is not.

113
00:06:45,090 --> 00:06:47,293
The habit does not announce itself.

114
00:06:47,373 --> 00:06:48,964
It does not feel like a view.

115
00:06:49,044 --> 00:06:51,007
It feels like the world itself.

116
00:06:51,825 --> 00:06:56,188
It is only when it is challenged by
Nāgārjuna's verses that these habits are

117
00:06:56,268 --> 00:06:57,913
brought to the surface.

118
00:06:57,993 --> 00:06:59,910
That is what the logic is for.

119
00:06:59,990 --> 00:07:03,076
Not to give a better taste,
but to bring out the habit,

120
00:07:03,156 --> 00:07:06,070
and then to unwind it, case by case.

121
00:07:06,877 --> 00:07:09,134
The logic does not do this alone.

122
00:07:09,214 --> 00:07:11,212
The habit is deeper than thought.

123
00:07:11,292 --> 00:07:14,066
It is in perception, and even in the body.

124
00:07:14,146 --> 00:07:17,123
What the logic does is
point to the place to look.

125
00:07:17,203 --> 00:07:19,772
Then I look, and check
it against the taste.

126
00:07:19,852 --> 00:07:22,327
Is a whole found apart from its parts?

127
00:07:22,407 --> 00:07:24,066
Is a cause found pushing?

128
00:07:24,146 --> 00:07:27,693
Each time the answer is
seen, not only agreed to,

129
00:07:27,773 --> 00:07:29,600
the habit loosens a little.

130
00:07:30,401 --> 00:07:33,840
Insight without the logic
drifts back into nouns.

131
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:37,988
Logic without the taste stays
a clever argument about words.

132
00:07:38,805 --> 00:07:43,847
Nāgārjuna makes the same move
as anatta, again and again.

133
00:07:43,927 --> 00:07:48,304
There is no seer, either bound
up with seeing or apart from it.

134
00:07:48,384 --> 00:07:49,843
A goer does not go.

135
00:07:49,973 --> 00:07:53,575
Fire is neither the same as
its fuel nor other than it.

136
00:07:53,655 --> 00:07:57,040
And in his first chapter he
takes the doer out of causes.

137
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:59,554
A self is the doer behind the doing.

138
00:07:59,634 --> 00:08:04,028
A causal power is the doer behind
the causing. Neither is found.

139
00:08:04,862 --> 00:08:08,496
Before freedom, the mind
always hinges on something.

140
00:08:09,333 --> 00:08:11,074
First it hinges on parts.

141
00:08:11,154 --> 00:08:13,126
A thing is made of its pieces.

142
00:08:13,206 --> 00:08:17,895
When the parts are seen through, it
does not let go. It hinges on the whole.

143
00:08:17,975 --> 00:08:21,414
When the whole is seen through,
it finds something finer.

144
00:08:21,494 --> 00:08:25,925
Qi, energy, a field,
relations, a substrate.

145
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:28,891
Each time, it is looking for a foundation.

146
00:08:29,710 --> 00:08:32,090
The tools meet each hinge in turn.

147
00:08:32,170 --> 00:08:36,329
The chariot is not found among
its parts, nor apart from them.

148
00:08:36,409 --> 00:08:40,323
Energy is singled out and
designated like everything else.

149
00:08:40,403 --> 00:08:43,693
A field is the whole
again, in a softer form.

150
00:08:43,773 --> 00:08:45,663
Relations are not found either.

151
00:08:45,743 --> 00:08:49,970
And a substrate is the foundation
the mind was looking for all along.

152
00:08:50,050 --> 00:08:51,401
It is not found.

153
00:08:52,226 --> 00:08:56,059
When all of these are exhausted,
with nothing left to hinge on,

154
00:08:56,139 --> 00:09:01,141
the mind becomes free from all
elaborations, and in a stable way.

155
00:09:01,221 --> 00:09:04,171
Stable does not mean the
habit can never stir.

156
00:09:04,251 --> 00:09:06,997
It means the freedom no
longer needs looking,

157
00:09:07,077 --> 00:09:09,053
or effort, to be there.

158
00:09:09,857 --> 00:09:13,269
Then appearance is again
tasted as vividly present,

159
00:09:13,349 --> 00:09:15,361
spontaneous and free.

160
00:09:15,441 --> 00:09:18,151
This is the first taste, revisited.

161
00:09:18,957 --> 00:09:23,157
It is the same taste. What has changed
is the understanding around it,

162
00:09:23,237 --> 00:09:28,116
and two things more. Reach: at
first the taste lived in the senses.

163
00:09:28,196 --> 00:09:33,782
Now it covers thought, the body,
things, causes, time and death.

164
00:09:33,862 --> 00:09:38,143
And stability: at first the habit
took it back when I stopped looking.

165
00:09:38,223 --> 00:09:40,321
Now it no longer depends on looking.

166
00:09:41,150 --> 00:09:45,432
Take away the doer from everything,
and put nothing in its place.

167
00:09:45,512 --> 00:09:50,826
No seer, no producing cause, and not
even dependence kept as a new thing.

168
00:09:50,906 --> 00:09:52,972
Then nothing is making the appearing.

169
00:09:53,052 --> 00:09:55,839
The sound of a car going
by is not a product.

170
00:09:55,919 --> 00:10:00,490
It shows up whole and vivid,
exactly as its conditions meet.

171
00:10:01,314 --> 00:10:05,623
That is what spontaneous presence
means to me. It is not uncaused.

172
00:10:05,703 --> 00:10:09,441
Every appearing has its
conditions. And it is not a source.

173
00:10:09,521 --> 00:10:12,579
Nothing stands behind
appearing, giving it off.

174
00:10:12,659 --> 00:10:15,963
Mind and matter lose their
weight, and become light,

175
00:10:16,043 --> 00:10:18,032
magical and plastic.

176
00:10:18,849 --> 00:10:22,401
Then I re-enter the
marketplace, and dirty my hands.

177
00:10:23,234 --> 00:10:25,899
The marketplace is ordinary life.

178
00:10:25,979 --> 00:10:30,546
Work, family, money, arguments,
other people's troubles,

179
00:10:30,626 --> 00:10:32,502
choices that have to be made.

180
00:10:32,582 --> 00:10:35,804
The last of the Zen
ox-herding pictures shows it:

181
00:10:35,884 --> 00:10:41,171
barefoot, smeared with mud and ashes, he
comes into the market with helping hands,

182
00:10:41,251 --> 00:10:42,451
smiling.

183
00:10:43,052 --> 00:10:45,648
Here dependent arising changes its role.

184
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:49,127
Before, it was the tool
that took each hinge apart.

185
00:10:49,207 --> 00:10:52,252
Now I deal in causes
and conditions all day:

186
00:10:52,332 --> 00:10:55,716
what helps, what harms,
what follows from what.

187
00:10:55,796 --> 00:10:58,411
Dependent arising is how help works.

188
00:10:59,242 --> 00:11:01,391
Who decides, if no one is there?

189
00:11:01,471 --> 00:11:03,116
Nobody disappears.

190
00:11:03,196 --> 00:11:08,116
I still act, choose, keep my
promises and answer for what I do,

191
00:11:08,196 --> 00:11:09,882
as a conventional person.

192
00:11:09,962 --> 00:11:13,768
What is gone is the doer behind
the doing, pulling the levers.

193
00:11:13,848 --> 00:11:18,786
Responsibility is answered first,
and nothing in the taste cancels it.

194
00:11:19,585 --> 00:11:22,331
And why help, if others are not found?

195
00:11:22,411 --> 00:11:26,556
Their suffering still functions,
and it arises in dependence.

196
00:11:26,636 --> 00:11:29,505
Because it is not fixed, it can be eased.

197
00:11:29,585 --> 00:11:33,069
A suffering that stood by
itself could not be touched.

198
00:11:33,869 --> 00:11:38,055
So, looked back on, the taste
has been met three times.

199
00:11:38,135 --> 00:11:39,894
Anatta, in seeing.

200
00:11:40,037 --> 00:11:44,930
Freedom from all elaborations,
when every hinge is exhausted.

201
00:11:45,010 --> 00:11:49,251
And dependent arising and
emptiness, in the marketplace.

202
00:11:49,331 --> 00:11:51,234
In the taste there is no order.

203
00:11:51,314 --> 00:11:55,097
In a life there is one, and
it goes round more than once.

204
00:11:55,905 --> 00:11:57,105
Now the map.

205
00:11:58,490 --> 00:12:00,734
Three descriptions, one taste.

206
00:12:00,814 --> 00:12:03,193
Anatta: no one is behind it.

207
00:12:03,273 --> 00:12:05,802
Not a blank; nobody disappears.

208
00:12:05,882 --> 00:12:09,524
Dependent arising: nothing
in it stands on its own.

209
00:12:09,604 --> 00:12:11,671
Not a web, and not a ground.

210
00:12:11,751 --> 00:12:14,986
Spontaneous presence: nothing is missing,

211
00:12:15,066 --> 00:12:16,780
and nothing is making it.

212
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:19,298
Not uncaused, and not a source.

213
00:12:20,105 --> 00:12:25,555
None is higher. They are not a lower
truth and a higher one, and not stages.

214
00:12:25,635 --> 00:12:27,688
Nor does one turn into another.

215
00:12:27,768 --> 00:12:32,063
I do not say dependent arising
becomes spontaneous presence,

216
00:12:32,143 --> 00:12:36,266
any more than we say summer
becomes winter. Nothing crosses.

217
00:12:37,090 --> 00:12:41,684
And anatta, read as a seal and
not only as the first insight,

218
00:12:41,764 --> 00:12:45,950
says the same of everything:
all things are without self.

219
00:12:46,030 --> 00:12:50,950
Not only no seer behind seeing,
but no self-nature in the seen,

220
00:12:51,030 --> 00:12:53,292
in the cause, in the condition.

221
00:12:54,110 --> 00:12:56,408
The descriptions keep each other honest.

222
00:12:56,488 --> 00:13:01,530
Dependent arising keeps spontaneous
presence from being heard as coming from a

223
00:13:01,610 --> 00:13:02,794
hidden ground.

224
00:13:02,874 --> 00:13:08,242
Spontaneous presence keeps dependent
arising from being heard as a machine of

225
00:13:08,322 --> 00:13:10,461
causes working in the dark.

226
00:13:11,274 --> 00:13:14,577
Dependent arising lives
in the default framework:

227
00:13:14,657 --> 00:13:18,096
the everyday cutting of the
appearing into parts and whole,

228
00:13:18,176 --> 00:13:22,648
before and after, cause and
effect. That framework works.

229
00:13:22,728 --> 00:13:26,307
We need it to speak, to
cook and to keep promises.

230
00:13:27,118 --> 00:13:29,090
The framework is not the prison.

231
00:13:29,170 --> 00:13:32,337
What binds is living in
it with reified thoughts,

232
00:13:32,417 --> 00:13:36,603
taking the parts and the conditions
to be there from their own side.

233
00:13:36,683 --> 00:13:38,628
That habit is the matrix.

234
00:13:38,708 --> 00:13:41,563
Dependent arising is not the matrix.

235
00:13:41,643 --> 00:13:44,516
It is the wisdom that shows the matrix up.

236
00:13:45,338 --> 00:13:48,573
Without the framework, there
is one complete stroke.

237
00:13:48,653 --> 00:13:50,462
One here does not mean one stuff.

238
00:13:50,542 --> 00:13:54,362
It means not cut into before
and after, parts and whole.

239
00:13:54,442 --> 00:13:58,007
The colour is still the colour,
and the sound still the sound.

240
00:13:58,885 --> 00:14:02,786
Freedom from all elaborations
is known without the cutting.

241
00:14:02,866 --> 00:14:04,688
That does not mean somewhere else.

242
00:14:04,768 --> 00:14:08,275
It is the same appearing,
known without concepts.

243
00:14:08,355 --> 00:14:12,994
That is why it can go back to work in the
marketplace without becoming a refuge.

244
00:14:13,797 --> 00:14:17,412
And from the taste, I
recognise its many faces.

245
00:14:17,492 --> 00:14:22,480
A sound, a thought, a flash of
anger, a cause and its effect,

246
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:25,379
a stretch of time, washing the dishes.

247
00:14:26,185 --> 00:14:30,670
A death, too. Conventionally someone
has died, and that is mourned.

248
00:14:30,750 --> 00:14:35,534
But no one is found who goes, and nothing
that was there by itself is cut off.

249
00:14:35,614 --> 00:14:39,261
The grief, vivid as it
is, has nothing behind it.

250
00:14:40,061 --> 00:14:43,119
It is much like a model
that recognises faces.

251
00:14:43,199 --> 00:14:46,842
It knows a face across
light, angle and age,

252
00:14:46,922 --> 00:14:51,869
not because it stored one photograph, but
because it learned the face's structure.

253
00:14:51,949 --> 00:14:57,526
A sameness of structure. Once the taste
is known, it is recognised by its shape.

254
00:14:58,329 --> 00:15:00,368
The shape is the same each time.

255
00:15:00,448 --> 00:15:04,974
No one behind it, nothing standing
on its own, nothing missing.

256
00:15:05,054 --> 00:15:08,629
Not the same stuff carried
from one situation to the next.

257
00:15:08,709 --> 00:15:12,338
If the taste became an
essence present in everything,

258
00:15:12,418 --> 00:15:14,077
it would be the ground again.

259
00:15:14,157 --> 00:15:16,211
And no one is doing the recognising.

260
00:15:16,291 --> 00:15:20,835
That too is an appearing, with
no recogniser standing behind it.

261
00:15:21,637 --> 00:15:23,500
Recognition can misfire.

262
00:15:23,580 --> 00:15:28,572
The I AM presence, a blank
quiet, a refined oneness:

263
00:15:28,675 --> 00:15:32,141
each can look like the
taste. The test is the shape.

264
00:15:32,221 --> 00:15:35,823
Is a witness, a source or
a background still left?

265
00:15:35,903 --> 00:15:37,567
Is something being kept up?

266
00:15:38,369 --> 00:15:42,256
In fact, every mistake on
this path has the same shape:

267
00:15:42,336 --> 00:15:46,038
the doer, put back somewhere
else, in a bigger coat.

268
00:15:46,845 --> 00:15:51,357
After anatta, a vast Awareness
in which everything happens.

269
00:15:51,437 --> 00:15:57,091
In total exertion, a cosmic whole, or
a substrate flowing under the verbs.

270
00:15:57,171 --> 00:16:01,411
In dependent arising, a web
or a mechanism behind things.

271
00:16:01,491 --> 00:16:05,909
In spontaneous presence, a source
that gives off appearances,

272
00:16:05,989 --> 00:16:08,354
or appearances without causes.

273
00:16:08,434 --> 00:16:11,642
In the marketplace, the
saviour who has arrived,

274
00:16:11,722 --> 00:16:14,550
or the bystander who says it is all empty,

275
00:16:14,630 --> 00:16:16,357
so nothing needs doing.

276
00:16:16,437 --> 00:16:18,925
And in practice, a state to keep up.

277
00:16:19,005 --> 00:16:23,789
Maintenance would be the split again.
None of this is kept. It was always so.

278
00:16:23,869 --> 00:16:25,261
It is recognised.

279
00:16:26,065 --> 00:16:28,254
Do I depart from the great masters?

280
00:16:28,334 --> 00:16:30,690
At the core, I do not believe so.

281
00:16:31,493 --> 00:16:36,902
Nāgārjuna praises dependent arising as
without arising and without ceasing.

282
00:16:36,982 --> 00:16:40,910
What arises in dependence does
not arise from its own side.

283
00:16:40,990 --> 00:16:46,073
Dzogchen says spontaneous presence
is not made by causes and conditions.

284
00:16:46,153 --> 00:16:49,990
I read that as Nāgārjuna's
"unborn by nature":

285
00:16:50,134 --> 00:16:53,618
appearing through conditions,
yet nothing produced.

286
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:56,162
Where I part, I say so.

287
00:16:56,251 --> 00:16:59,255
From Tsongkhapa, on the order of the path:

288
00:16:59,335 --> 00:17:03,304
mine was the taste first, and
the view syncing with it later.

289
00:17:03,384 --> 00:17:08,875
On the bridge across time: I keep neither
carried nor cut, with no link needed.

290
00:17:08,955 --> 00:17:12,040
And from the reading of
Indra's net as the real:

291
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:16,348
nothing stands alone, but the
relations are not found either.

292
00:17:16,428 --> 00:17:17,761
These are my readings.

293
00:17:17,841 --> 00:17:22,222
Some lineages see it differently, and
you should read them for yourself.

294
00:17:23,029 --> 00:17:25,589
Try it. Listen to a sound nearby.

295
00:17:26,393 --> 00:17:28,432
Look for the hearer behind the hearing.

296
00:17:28,512 --> 00:17:30,321
Then look at the hearing itself.

297
00:17:30,401 --> 00:17:35,257
Is a process running underneath, or
just sound, with no effort at all?

298
00:17:36,069 --> 00:17:37,891
Now look for what makes the sound.

299
00:17:37,971 --> 00:17:41,695
The engine, the air,
the ear, the attention.

300
00:17:41,775 --> 00:17:44,906
Is any of them standing
behind it, pushing it out?

301
00:17:45,734 --> 00:17:50,627
Then stop looking. The sound is
complete, exactly as its conditions meet.

302
00:17:50,707 --> 00:17:55,238
Do not try to keep this. When the
next sound comes, it is complete too.

303
00:17:56,045 --> 00:17:59,470
No one behind it, nothing
standing on its own,

304
00:17:59,550 --> 00:18:03,496
nothing missing: one
taste, met again and again.

